'''‡''' 2010 brings two US Senate elections to New York, [[Chuck Schumer|Charles Schumer]]'s seat is considered a safe Democrat hold by all sources listed in the table. (The senator is seeking reelection to a third term.) The seat held by [[Kirsten Gillibrand]] is listed as New York*, with an [[asterisk]].

Aggregate analysis using individual races on [[Intrade.com]] shows that Democrats are predicted to have an 86% chance of retaining their majority. However, Republicans are expected to pick between 7 and eight seats. <ref>{{cite web|author=Pollstered.com|url=http://www.pollstered.blogspot.com/|title=2010  |publisher=http://www.pollstered.blogspot.com/|date=2010-10-13 |accessdate=2010-10-13 }}</ref>


