*Former Speaker of the [[Florida House of Representatives]] [[Marco Rubio]] is running and positioning himself as a more conservative candidate than Crist. Opinion polls suggested that Rubio had overtaken Crist and held a large advantage among GOP primary voters.<ref name=rubio>{{cite web | url = http://www.miamiherald.com/news/florida/AP/story/1032966.html |title=Former Fla. Speaker Rubio will seek US Senate seat |author=Brendan Farrington |accessdate=May 12, 2009}} {{Dead link|date=September 2010|bot=H3llBot}}</ref> In late April, Crist decided to run as an independent.

Rubio was joined by nine other Republicans vying for the GOP nomination.<ref name="thegreenpapers2">{{cite web|url=http://www.thegreenpapers.com/G10/FL |title=Florida 2010 Midterm Election |publisher=Thegreenpapers.com |date= |accessdate=2010-06-13}}</ref> However, he won the nomination on August 24, 2010 without the need for a runoff.

'''Announced Democratic candidates'''
*U.S. Representative [[Kendrick Meek]] of [[FL-17|Florida's 17th congressional district]]<ref name="Meek">{{cite news | work=USA Today | url=http://www.usatoday.com/news/politics/2009-01-12-meek_N.htm | title=Fla. Rep. Meek to run for Senate | date=January 12, 2009 | accessdate=May 27, 2010}}</ref>
*[[Mayor]] [[Kevin Burns (Florida)|Kevin Burns]] ([[North Miami, Florida|North Miami]])<ref name="Burns">{{cite web | url=http://www.sun-sentinel.com/news/local/breakingnews/sfl-bn-0217burns,0,3517473.story | work= sun-sentinel.com | title=Mayor of North Miami to seek U.S. Senate seat}}</ref>
*Pastor Tyrone Brown<ref name="BrownMcClellanCoggins">{{cite web | title=Former Shores councilman declares run for mayor | url=http://www.news-journalonline.com/NewsJournalOnline/News/EastVolusia/evlEAST03POL032309.htm | work= journalonline.com}}{{dead link|date=October 2010}}</ref>
*[[Key West, Florida|Key West]] resident "Trinidad Joe" Allen<ref name="Trinidad Joe">{{cite web | url=http://www.keysnet.com/news/story/88813.html | work= Keysnet.com  | title=Key Wester Trinidad Joe eyes U.S. Senate seat}}{{dead link|date=October 2010}}</ref>
*[[Jeff Greene]], a billionaire real estate executive<ref>{{cite news|last=Finn |first=Tyler |url=http://www.cbsnews.com/8301-503544_162-20003875-503544.html |title=Billionaire Democrat Jeff Greene Joins Florida Senate Race - Political Hotsheet |publisher=CBS News |date=2010-04-30 |accessdate=2010-06-13}}</ref>

They were joined by four other Democrats seeking the nomination.<ref name="thegreenpapers2"/> However, Kendrick Meek won the Democratic nomination on the twenty-fourth of August.

