{{Main|United States Senate election in Ohio, 2010}}
Two-term incumbent Republican [[George Voinovich]] was reelected with 64 percent of the vote in 2004. Voinovich, the former Mayor of [[Cleveland, Ohio|Cleveland]], [[Lieutenant Governor of Ohio|Lieutenant Governor]] and [[Governor of Ohio|Governor]], announced his intention to retire rather than seek reelection to a third term in 2010.<ref name="Voinovich 2010">[http://blog.cleveland.com/openers/2009/01/its_official_voinovich_to_reti.html It's Official Voinovich To Retire], cleveland.com</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.politico.com/news/stories/0109/17324.html | title=Voinovich to announce retirement | publisher = [[Politico (newspaper)|Politico]] | date = January 11, 2009}}</ref>

