====Daniel Inouye of Hawaii====
{{Main|United States Senate election in Hawaii, 2010}}
Eight-term incumbent Democrat [[Daniel Inouye]] was reelected with 76 percent of the vote in 2004<ref name=nyt_west>{{cite news|url=http://query.nytimes.com/gst/fullpage.html?res=9D00E4DF173CF937A35752C1A9629C8B63&sec=&spon=&pagewanted=all |title=The 2004 Elections: State by State -- West |work=[[The New York Times]] |date=2004-11-04 | accessdate=2008-11-06 | first1=Contributing | last1=To | first2=Patrick | last2=Healy | first3=Michael | last3=Janofsky | first4=Michael | last4=Luo | first5=Jennifer | last5=Medina | first6=Robert | last6=Pear | first7=Richard | last7=Prez-Pea | first8=Marc | last8=Santora | first9=Stephanie | last9=Strom | first10=Daniel J. | last10=Wakin}}</ref> and has announced that he will seek another term.<ref name="Inouye 2010">{{cite web | url= http://news.yahoo.com/s/cq/20081211/pl_cq_politics/politics2996751 | title= Eight-Term Hawaii Sen. Inouye Seeks Re-Election in 2010 | publisher = Yahoo News | date = 2008-12-11 | accessdate=2008-12-11}} {{Dead link|date=September 2010|bot=H3llBot}}</ref>

